GameDrop — Windsurf rules (authoritative set: AGENTS.md)

PROJECT
- Headless Go free-game collector. One process invocation = one collection cycle
  (fetch Steam/Epic/GOG → persist SQLite → Telegram outbox → exit).
- Deployed as one Fly.io Scheduled Machine with one Fly Volume. No server, no API,
  no UI, no in-app scheduler. Never introduce one.

STRUCTURE
- cmd/gamedrop: wiring + exit codes only (0 ok/partial, 1 failure, 2 bad config).
- internal/stores/<store>: adapter parsing/classification only; never imports
  storage or notify.
- internal/storage: SQLite, migrations, transactions, outbox rows.
- internal/collector: orchestration, concurrency, expiry, notification policy.
- internal/notify: rendering, Telegram sender, outbox processor.

HARD RULES
- free_to_keep requires verified 100% discount from a non-zero original price;
  otherwise unknown or skip. Never classify from a zero price alone.
- Zero time.Time means unknown; never invent starts/ends.
- Absent from a scan → mark missing only. Expiry requires a passed ends_at.
- Failed/partial source writes nothing; previous data is preserved.
- Offer identity is (store, country, store_offer_id); never dedupe by title.
- Notifications: transactional outbox, at-least-once, dedupe keys; do not claim
  exactly-once.
- Only dependency: modernc.org/sqlite. .env loading is built in (internal/envfile,
  real env wins); no dotenv package, no PostgreSQL, no broker.
- Never log or commit secrets (tokens, chat IDs, cookies, .env).
- English in code, comments, tests, docs.

STYLE
- gofmt clean, go vet clean, %w-wrapped errors, context propagated, structured
  slog with stable keys, no global mutable state.

TESTS
- Offline only: httptest + testdata fixtures, t.TempDir() databases, injected
  clocks. Add a fixture regression test with every parser fix.

VERIFY
- gofmt -l . (empty), go vet ./..., go test ./..., go build ./...

Do not commit, push, or deploy unless the user explicitly asks.
